The display is in the **Dinosaur Court (Geological Court) at Crystal Palace Park, south London, England**. The partly submerged animal is **_Mosasaurus_**—not technically a dinosaur, but a large extinct marine lizard. It lies in the lake near the secondary island, with only its head and part of its back visible.

Hawkins and Richard Owen had only a _Mosasaurus_ skull to work from, so they did not know the animal’s full shape. Later fossil discoveries showed that it had:

- a long, streamlined, lizard-like body;
- four paddle-shaped limbs;
- a long, powerful tail ending in a vertically flattened, two-lobed tail fluke.

Thus, the unseen portion would have looked broadly like the body of a huge marine monitor lizard or sea serpent with four flippers and a broad swimming tail—not the squat, fully terrestrial form suggested by many of the other Crystal Palace reconstructions.
